From 2c92fdd227df66bff2422eae56c7b53265bc0577 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew <matthewhale@live.com.au>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 09:08:19 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 01/59] Widescreen cockpit, edge HUD, XvT gunnery/throttle,
 lasers+ions link, wreck flip fix

- collide.c: halve the detached-component yaw offset as a signed value. The
  unsigned shift turned a negative offset into a ~170 degree flip, sending
  wrecks back into the pursuing player.
- render.cockpit_stretch: the 4:3 cockpit art spans the window and the world
  shows on both sides.
- render.hud_widescreen: in cockpit-off views, side HUD panes move to the
  screen edges (per pane; the message strip stays centered).
- game.laser_convergence_metres: convergence at the target's range within
  30 degrees and 0.02-2.5 km, otherwise at this distance.
- game.xvt_lasers: XvT cannon refire (47 ticks) and bolts at 2x speed for
  half the lifetime; HUD in-range prediction follows.
- game.xvt_throttle: XvT accel/decel rates and big-gap braking.
- game.ai_ion_link and the player X-key "lasers and ion cannons fire
  linked" step for craft with two cannon groups.
- Settings page entries for all of the above.
